    "rawContent": "---\nname: docx-architect\ndescription: Official Anthropic skill for creating, manipulating, and validating Microsoft Word (.docx) documents with strict OpenXML standards.\nmetadata:\n  author: Anthropic\n  version: 1.0.0\n---\n\n# Word Document (DOCX) Engineering Standards\n\nWhen generating or manipulating Word documents, adhere strictly to OpenXML packaging conventions:\n\n1. Document Hierarchy:\n   - Enforce document part relationships in `word/_rels/document.xml.rels`.\n   - Base all body content inside `w:document > w:body` elements.\n   - Use explicit `w:pStyle` definitions rather than manual inline font tags for headings.\n\n2. Typography & Formatting:\n   - Set standard font stacks with clear fallback families.\n   - Explicitly define paragraph spacing with `w:spacing w:after=\"160\" w:line=\"240\" w:lineRule=\"auto\"`.\n   - Never introduce orphan tables: always wrap tabular data inside standard `w:tbl` with explicit column widths (`w:tblGrid`).\n\n3. Tracked Changes Integrity:\n   - When editing existing legal or corporate documents, never delete previous authors' revisions.\n   - Wrap modifications in `w:ins` (insertion) and `w:del` (deletion) with unique incremental IDs and timestamps.\n\n4. Validation:\n   - Ensure all output packages are zipped with standard deflate compression and valid `[Content_Types].xml` definitions.",
