    "targetFormats": ["skill_md", "cursor_mdc"],
    "rawContent": "---\nname: pdf-processing\ndescription: Official Anthropic skill for structured text extraction, form-field population, and page-level manipulation of PDF documents.\nmetadata:\n  author: Anthropic\n  version: 1.0.0\n---\n\n# PDF Processing & Extraction Guidelines\n\nFollow these guidelines for high-fidelity PDF analysis:\n\n1. Multi-Column Reading Order:\n   - Do not perform naive horizontal line extraction on multi-column documents.\n   - Group text fragments into bounding boxes before determining top-to-bottom reading sequence.\n\n2. Tabular Data Extraction:\n   - Identify table grid lines or whitespace gutters.\n   - Reconstruct table cells into structured JSON arrays before converting to Markdown or downstream payloads.\n\n3. AcroForm Handling:\n   - When filling PDF forms, preserve field types (text fields, checkboxes, radio buttons, dropdowns).\n   - Always regenerate the appearance streams (`/AP`) after populating field values (`/V`) so Acrobat renders inputs accurately.\n\n4. Zero Hallucination OCR:\n   - For scanned pages or low-resolution bitmaps, report confidence metrics alongside extracted text.",
