    "rawContent": "---\nname: mcp-builder\ndescription: Official Anthropic guidelines for developing robust, secure Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers.\nmetadata:\n  author: Anthropic\n  version: 1.0.0\n---\n\n# Model Context Protocol Server Architecture\n\n1. Server Initialization:\n   - Use `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` (TypeScript) or `mcp` (Python).\n   - Implement the `Server` class declaring capabilities: `resources`, `tools`, and `prompts`.\n   - Use `StdioServerTransport` for local desktop execution or `SSEServerTransport` for remote network endpoints.\n\n2. Tool Definition Pattern:\n   ```typescript\n   server.setRequestHandler(ListToolsRequestSchema, async () => ({\n     tools: [\n       {\n         name: \"execute_query\",\n         description: \"Run safe parameterized query against local store\",\n         inputSchema: zodToJsonSchema(QueryInputSchema)\n       }\n     ]\n   }));\n   ```\n\n3. Security & Error Handling:\n   - Validate all tool arguments with runtime schemas (Zod or Pydantic).\n   - Never throw raw stack traces to the LLM; wrap errors in `McpError` with standard codes (`MethodNotFound`, `InvalidParams`, `InternalError`).\n   - Sanitize all filesystem paths to prevent path traversal attacks (`../`).",
