    "rawContent": "---\nname: supabase-security-rls\ndescription: Official Supabase rules for PostgreSQL Row Level Security and privilege containment.\nmetadata:\n  author: Supabase\n  version: 1.0.0\n---\n\n# Supabase PostgreSQL Row Level Security Manifest\n\n1. Mandatory Table Lockdown:\n   - Every public table MUST execute: `ALTER TABLE {table_name} ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`\n   - Tables without RLS are strictly rejected by security audit.\n\n2. Granular Policy Separation:\n   - Never write a single catch-all policy for `ALL` actions.\n   - Create separate explicit policies for `SELECT`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, and `DELETE`.\n   - Example:\n     ```sql\n     CREATE POLICY \"Users can read own records\"\n     ON public.profiles FOR SELECT\n     USING (auth.uid() = id);\n     ```\n\n3. Security Definer Containment:\n   - When writing `SECURITY DEFINER` functions, ALWAYS set an explicit search path:\n     ```sql\n     CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()\n     RETURNS trigger\n     LANGUAGE plpgsql\n     SECURITY DEFINER SET search_path = public\n     AS $$ ... $$;\n     ```",
