    "rawContent": "---\nname: stripe-payments-guard\ndescription: Official Stripe integration standards for safe payments, webhooks, and zero credential leakage.\nmetadata:\n  author: Stripe\n  version: 1.0.0\n---\n\n# Stripe Institutional Engineering Standards\n\n1. Cryptographic Webhook Verification:\n   - Always verify webhooks using the raw request buffer: `stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(rawBody, sig, webhookSecret)`.\n   - Never parse JSON prior to signature verification.\n   - Return HTTP 200 immediately before dispatching long-running asynchronous worker jobs.\n\n2. Mutation Idempotency:\n   - All calls to `paymentIntents.create`, `charges.create`, or `refunds.create` MUST pass an `idempotencyKey`:\n     ```typescript\n     await stripe.paymentIntents.create({ ... }, { idempotencyKey: orderId });\n     ```\n\n3. Credential Isolation:\n   - `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` (`sk_live_...`) MUST NEVER be prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` or bundled in client code.\n   - Only `STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (`pk_...`) may be exposed to the browser.",
