    "rawContent": "---\ndescription: Strict TypeScript architecture rules\nglobs: **/*.{ts,tsx}\nalwaysApply: true\n---\n# TypeScript Strict Rules\n\n1. Zero `any` Rule:\n   - `any` is strictly prohibited. Use `unknown` and narrow with type guards or Zod schemas.\n\n2. Discriminated Unions:\n   - Model network states with explicit tags:\n     ```typescript\n     type AsyncData<T> =\n       | { status: 'idle' }\n       | { status: 'loading' }\n       | { status: 'success'; data: T }\n       | { status: 'error'; error: Error };\n     ```\n\n3. Exhaustiveness Checking:\n   - Always assert unhandled union branches with `assertNever(x: never): never` in default cases.",
